{"name":"Cafe Royale","hex":"#6a4928","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cafe royale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of café royale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cafe_royale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffeehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A coffeehouse, coffee shop, or café, is an establishment that serves various types of coffee drinks like espresso, latte, americano and cappuccino, as well as other beverages. An espresso bar specializes in serving espresso and espresso-based drinks. Some coffeehouses may serve iced coffee among other cold drinks, as well as non-caffeinated drinks. A coffeehouse may also serve food, such as light snacks, sandwiches, muffins, cakes, breads, pastries or doughnuts. Many doughnut shops in Canada and the U.S. serve coffee to accompany doughnuts, so these can also be classified as coffee shops, although doughnut shops tend to be more casual and serve cheaper fare. In continental Europe, some cafés even serve alcoholic drinks, and in West Asia, coffeehouses may offer a flavored tobacco smoked through a hookah, called shisha in most varieties of Arabic or nargile in Levantine Arabic, Greek, and Turkish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffeehouse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/500px-Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/1280px-Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Pale